<div id="recipe-88294-notes" class="wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Notes</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-notes"><span style="display: block;"><strong>Storing leftovers:</strong> This pasta recipe is best on the day it is made, but leftovers can be stored for up to 3 days. Bring the pasta to room temperature, place in an airtight container, and store it in the fridge.</span><div class="wprm-spacer"></div>
<span style="display: block;"><strong>Reheating:</strong> Warm it in a large skillet with a splash of water to keep the pasta moist. Keep in mind that chunks of burrata may melt a little, but it should still taste good. Alternatively, you can warm it in the microwave, but again, it is best to add a splash of water to prevent the pasta from drying out.</span><div class="wprm-spacer"></div>
<span style="display: block;">&nbsp;</span></div></div>
